   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize and direct the commissioner of agriculture and markets to\nconduct a study on vertical farming",
    "basePrintNo": "S4769",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4769-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4769\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize and direct the commissioner of agriculture and\nmarkets to conduct a study on vertical farming\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo examine the effects vertical farming would have on access to locally\ngrown food, job creation, educational opportunities, and the environ-\nment.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill directs the commissioner of agriculture and markets to conduct\na study on vertical farming. It also requires the commissioner to make\nrecommendations for legislation and administrative programs one year\nafter the act become effective.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nResidents in some parts of New York State do not have access to fresh\nproduce in their communities and must either travel far distances for it\nor do without. This legislation seeks to examine how vertical farming\nmight address the issue of food deserts in the state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: S5134 - Referred to Agriculture\n\n2023-24: S2414 - Referred to Agriculture\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
